fastjsonschema-rust attribution and scope
===========================================

This project is a standalone Rust port of the validation kernel of
`fastjsonschema`. It is BSD-3-Clause licensed (see LICENSE); it vendors
no upstream code.

Behavior, keyword semantics, error-message texts and paths, and the
`compile` / `compile_to_code` / `validate` entry-point shapes are
modelled on:

  horejsek/python-fastjsonschema — https://github.com/horejsek/python-fastjsonschema
  Copyright (c) 2018, Michal Horejsek; BSD-3-Clause
  (see https://github.com/horejsek/python-fastjsonschema/blob/master/LICENSE).

Ported against fastjsonschema 2.22.2. The `fastjsonschema` package
itself is a runtime dependency (it provides the exception classes the
Rust kernel raises, the `compile_to_code` entry point, and the
pure-Python fallback path); it is not vendored here.

`tests/corpus/*` are original fixtures written for this port (not
copied from the upstream test suite). The equivalence harness and the
upstream-suite gate compare against the installed `fastjsonschema`
package only at test time.
